<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Boris Godunov</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1552–1605</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Boris Godunov was regent of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> under the feeble <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tsar">Tsar</a> Feodor I and, after Feodor's death ended the Rurikid line in 1598, was elected tsar by an assembly of the land. As regent he oversaw the creation of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a> Patriarchate in 1589, and he pressed expansion into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siberia">Siberia</a>, but the great famine of 1601–1603 and the appearance of the pretender False Dmitry undermined his rule. His death in 1605 deepened the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/time-of-troubles">Time of Troubles</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/boris-godunov.jpg" alt="Boris Godunov" width="320" height="425" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Boris_Godunov.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
